{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00786",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.93,
      "end_seconds": 15.14,
      "duration_seconds": 14.21,
      "text": "Hi. Mum said I had to come on my own, because she's at work and I'm fifteen. I've got chickenpox. At least I think so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.13,
      "end_seconds": 25.55,
      "duration_seconds": 8.42,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll make sure we talk through everything. When did the spots start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.85,
      "end_seconds": 33.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.84,
      "text": "Three days ago. Now they're all over, but nothing in my mouth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.19,
      "end_seconds": 38.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Any fever or feeling unwell?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.13,
      "end_seconds": 48.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "Yeah, I had a temperature the first day, and a headache. Not now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.39,
      "end_seconds": 60.08,
      "duration_seconds": 8.69,
      "text": "And what's been done about it so far? Let me go through what you're using."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.64,
      "end_seconds": 83.66,
      "duration_seconds": 21.02,
      "text": "Calamine lotion, on the spots. Paracetamol, 500 mg, when I'm hot, maybe three a day. Cetirizine, 10 mg at night, so I can sleep. My inhaler, the blue one, when I wheeze. And emollient cream, for my eczema, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.15,
      "end_seconds": 93.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "That's a lot, and it sounds sensible. Any conditions apart from the chickenpox?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.36,
      "end_seconds": 97.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Asthma, and eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.77,
      "end_seconds": 100.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Any operations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.56,
      "end_seconds": 107.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Just my tonsils, when I was eight."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.38,
      "end_seconds": 114.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Do you do sport, or go out anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.67,
      "end_seconds": 121.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "I play netball. But obviously not now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.15,
      "end_seconds": 128.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.09,
      "end_seconds": 134.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "No. None that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.33,
      "end_seconds": 140.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Good. Let me look at your spots. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.81,
      "end_seconds": 158.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "They're everywhere."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.8,
      "end_seconds": 171.73,
      "duration_seconds": 10.93,
      "text": "There are red spots and blisters in different stages, some scabbed, over your chest, back and arms, and none look infected."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.38,
      "end_seconds": 177.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Is it definitely chickenpox? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.64,
      "end_seconds": 181.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Yes, the pattern is typical."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.78,
      "end_seconds": 189.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Oh good. Am I contagious? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.09,
      "end_seconds": 198.2,
      "duration_seconds": 8.11,
      "text": "Until every spot has scabbed over, usually about five days after the spots began, so stay home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.34,
      "end_seconds": 204.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "When can I go back to school? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.26,
      "end_seconds": 216.4,
      "duration_seconds": 11.14,
      "text": "When all the spots have crusted over. Don't go near anyone who's pregnant, or has a weak immune system, or a newborn. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.42,
      "end_seconds": 221.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "My auntie is pregnant. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.29,
      "end_seconds": 228.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Keep away from her until you're better."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.34,
      "end_seconds": 232.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.31,
      "end_seconds": 246.69,
      "duration_seconds": 12.38,
      "text": "Keep taking the paracetamol, but avoid ibuprofen, it can make chickenpox skin infections worse, and with asthma, it's best avoided."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.77,
      "end_seconds": 250.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.93,
      "end_seconds": 257.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "And keep your nails short. Try not to scratch. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.27,
      "end_seconds": 262.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "It's so itchy though. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.53,
      "end_seconds": 273.11,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "The cetirizine and the calamine are the right things. Cool baths help too. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.39,
      "end_seconds": 277.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Will they scar? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.66,
      "end_seconds": 283.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "If you don't scratch, most don't. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.42,
      "end_seconds": 287.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.07,
      "end_seconds": 301.1,
      "duration_seconds": 12.03,
      "text": "Come back if the spots become red, swollen and sore, you get a high fever, breathing problems, or you can't keep fluids down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.41,
      "end_seconds": 305.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "I will. Thanks. ~"
    }
  ]
}
